  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "59dd3c1baec62589319b23a201dd1d6ed240cbc8",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2017978984,
          "type": null,
          "body": "From the link: \"When using SSL connections in this style the client is required to use the ALPN extension defined by RFC 7301 to protect against protocol confusion attacks. The PostgreSQL protocol is \"postgresql\" as registered at IANA TLS ALPN Protocol IDs registry.\"\n\nWould it make more sense to register the ALPN via\n`dissector_add_string(\"tls.alpn\", \"postgresql\", pgsql_handle);`\nin `proto_reg_handoff_pgsql(void)`?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-07-26T15:37:43.780Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-07-26T15:37:43.780Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 317693046,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 16612,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e0f2bf162c48cb9ee6e812e07c3b6f5f9dd563d7",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2017991371,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The approach with the ALPN would have the advantage of working without having to explicitly configure the port, and also would avoid confusion and misdissection in cases where the configured PGSQL port was used for something else. Of course if clients don't actually use the ALPN it wouldn't work, but the documentation seems clear.\n\nDo you have a sample capture?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
